From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:30:41 -0300
Subject: drm/virtio: make room for the stereo scanout command in a vbuffer

Every command a vbuffer carries is allocated inline, and
virtio_gpu_get_vbuf() refuses a command larger than MAX_INLINE_CMD_SIZE
(96 bytes, the size of struct virtio_gpu_set_scanout_blob) with a BUG_ON.
struct virtio_gpu_set_scanout_stereo grew to 104 bytes when it gained the
rectangles of the graphics and graphics-depth pictures of the L + depth +
graphics + graphics-depth structure, so the first modeset on a device
that offers VIRTIO_GPU_F_STEREO hits the BUG_ON: on QEMU with
virtio-gpu-pci,stereo=on the fbdev modeset at module load oopses in
virtio_gpu_cmd_set_scanout_stereo() (virtgpu_vq.c:126), before any stereo
mode is set.

Raise MAX_INLINE_CMD_SIZE to 104 and make a stereo command that does not
fit a build error instead of a runtime BUG.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vq.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vq.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vq.c
index 2f59b90552..95af694a74 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vq.c
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
 #include "virtgpu_drv.h"
 #include "virtgpu_trace.h"
 
-#define MAX_INLINE_CMD_SIZE   96
+#define MAX_INLINE_CMD_SIZE   104
 #define MAX_INLINE_RESP_SIZE  24
 #define VBUFFER_SIZE          (sizeof(struct virtio_gpu_vbuffer) \
 			       + MAX_INLINE_CMD_SIZE		 \
@@ -806,6 +806,7 @@ void virtio_gpu_cmd_set_scanout_stereo(struct virtio_gpu_device *vgdev,
 		break;
 	}
 
+	BUILD_BUG_ON(sizeof(*cmd_p) > MAX_INLINE_CMD_SIZE);
 	cmd_p = virtio_gpu_alloc_cmd(vgdev, &vbuf, sizeof(*cmd_p));
 	memset(cmd_p, 0, sizeof(*cmd_p));
 
